@startuml
title Dromos - Create an optimized route (up to 25 destinations)
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
boundary Browser
control RoutePlanController
control CreateOptimizedRoutePlan
control CachedGeocoder
database MySQL
participant "Google Geocoding API" as Geocoding
participant "RouteOptimizer" as Optimizer
participant "Google Routes API" as RoutesAPI

User -> Browser : Submit start, destinations and options
Browser -> RoutePlanController : POST /routes
RoutePlanController -> RoutePlanController : Validate request and destination limit
RoutePlanController -> CreateOptimizedRoutePlan : execute(validated input, user)

loop Start and every destination
  CreateOptimizedRoutePlan -> CachedGeocoder : geocode(full address)
  CachedGeocoder -> MySQL : find normalized address
  alt Cache hit
    MySQL --> CachedGeocoder : saved coordinates + Place ID
    CachedGeocoder -> MySQL : increment hit_count, update last_used_at
  else Cache miss
    CachedGeocoder -> Geocoding : geocode using server credential
    Geocoding --> CachedGeocoder : verified address + coordinates + Place ID
    CachedGeocoder -> MySQL : store reusable geocoding result
  end
  CachedGeocoder --> CreateOptimizedRoutePlan : geocoded location
end

CreateOptimizedRoutePlan -> Optimizer : optimize by driving time\n(options include toll avoidance/return)
Optimizer -> RoutesAPI : computeRoutes with waypoint optimization\nand traffic-aware routing
RoutesAPI --> Optimizer : optimized order, legs, totals, polyline
Optimizer --> CreateOptimizedRoutePlan : route result
CreateOptimizedRoutePlan -> MySQL : transaction: save route_plan + ordered stops
CreateOptimizedRoutePlan --> RoutePlanController : saved plan
RoutePlanController --> Browser : redirect to route workspace
Browser -> MySQL : page request loads saved data through Laravel
Browser -> Browser : render ordered list and stored road polyline

note over Browser,MySQL
  Refreshing an unchanged saved route reads the database;
  it does not geocode or calculate the route again.
end note
@enduml

